<title>ARGENTINA: Report warned of Argentine customs losses - paper.</title>
<headline>Report warned of Argentine customs losses - paper.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. consultancy warned the Argentine government in 1993 that it was losing $900 million a year from smuggling but its recommendations were ignored, La Nacion newspaper reported Monday.</p>
<p>In a report sponsored by the U.S. Trade Development Agency, Science Applications International warned of understaffing and inadequate infrastructure and recommended major changes to inspection procedures, La Naicion said.</p>
<p>President Carlos Menem announced a major investigation into corruption within the customs service in October and the government said it believes it has lost $10 billion in four years to an organized smuggling ring within the service.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
